miadi-server — the Miadi web app, built and ready to run

  sudo apt install miadi-server

The package holds the built app, its launcher and a per-user systemd unit. It
needs no checkout, no pnpm and no build on the host, and it starts nothing.

  miadi-server init /path/to/.env     # the app's settings, kept at mode 600
  miadi-server check                  # what would run and what stops it
  miadi-server                        # run it in the foreground on 127.0.0.1:3335
  systemctl --user enable --now miadi-server

`miadi-server --help` lists every command and setting.

Settings are in ~/.config/miadi-server/env. What the app saves goes in
~/.local/state/miadi-server, and is kept across upgrades.

The app has to reach a Redis (KV_REST_API_URL) and a medicine wheel
(MIADI_CHRONICLE_MW_URL), and `miadi-server check` says whether each answers.

Person and seat tokens are checked against credentials.jsonl in
MIADI_IDENTITY_DIR (default /srv/miadi/identity), a file local to each host.
A new host needs that file from the host that issued the tokens, or new
tokens from its own /me page. Shared reader and writer tokens need neither.

A host that runs the app from its own checkout sets MIADI_PROJECT_DIR, and the
launcher runs that checkout instead. Building a checkout needs pnpm and npm.

An exit status of 2 from miadi-server is a setup problem. The unit does not
restart on it, and `miadi-server check` names it.

Source: https://github.com/jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit, packages/miadi/deb
